# Vauxhall Zafira C (Zafira Tourer) seven-seat MPV, 2012-2018.
#
# The Zafira Tourer: the third-generation car, longer and lower than the B
# with the more sculpted body and the panoramic roof option. UK sales from
# March 2012.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Zafira
#
# Dimensions 4.660 x 1.820 x 1.690 m, wheelbase 2.760 m (Wikipedia infobox;
# the 1.884 m figure quoted elsewhere includes the door mirrors).
#
# Shape reference: the weakest of the Zafira packs. NO true level side
# elevation of a Zafira Tourer was found, so the flank is estimated within
# the published dimensions and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Zafira Tourer October 2011 brochure for model year
# 2012: Royal Blue solid, Power Red two-coat, Olympic White brilliant, and
# Sovereign Silver, Silver Lake, Silky Shadow, Technical Grey and Carbon
# Flash metallic. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
# Speed 205 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro March 2012; retires staggered 2018-2021 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-c.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-zafira-c.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-zafira-c/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the pre-facelift exterior represents the range. The
# windscreen is one continuous black surface and the panoramic option is not
# modelled separately. The side crease and the bumper sculpture are shallower
# than in the photographs.


obj=citycar
